          "content": "def max_non_overlapping(intervals):\n    # Return the largest number of mutually non-overlapping intervals.\n    # Intervals are (start, end) pairs and are half-open, so (0, 3) and\n    # (3, 5) do not overlap. Input order is arbitrary.\n    # Sort intervals so we can use a greedy strategy.\n    intervals.sort()\n    end = intervals[0][1]\n    count = 1\n\n    # Count how many of the intervals don't overlap with (0, end).\n    for interval in intervals[1:]:\n        if interval[0] >= end:\n            end = interval[1]\n            count += 1\n    return count",
